course: dictionary
lesson: 2836
title: Dizziness: a warning sign
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Dizziness is the feeling that you or the things around you are spinning, or that you might fall. It is a word you will meet in health and safety lessons, and in science too. Context tells you what it means: «Signs of concussion include headache, dizziness, feeling sick, blurred vision, confusion, forgetting things, wobbling and acting differently.» Dizziness sits in a list of body signs, so it is a sign that something is wrong in the body.
explain: Dizziness can come from many causes. You can feel it after spinning round, from standing up too fast, from being hot, hungry or ill, or after a knock on the head. «In hot weather children can become dehydrated quickly, with headache, tiredness and dizziness as the first signs.» Here, dizziness is an early warning that the body needs water.
explain: When you feel dizzy, act quickly. The sentence «In hot weather… then you stop, sit in the shade, drink water and tell an adult» gives the plan: stop, sit or lie down, drink water, and tell an adult. Do not keep playing and hope it passes.
fact: Dizziness is the feeling that you or things around you are spinning, or that you might fall.
fact: «Feel dizzy» means you have that spinning or wobbly feeling right now.
fact: «A spell of dizziness» means a short time when the dizzy feeling comes and goes.
fact: Dizziness can come from spinning round, standing up too fast, heat, hunger, illness, or a head injury.
fact: In science, the inner ear helps your balance. Spinning confuses it and causes dizziness.
exercise: «Signs of concussion include headache, dizziness, feeling sick, blurred vision, confusion, forgetting things, wobbling and acting differently.» What is dizziness? | Being very tired after a long lesson | A type of sweet cake | A loud noise in your ear | *The feeling that you or the things around you are spinning, or that you might fall
exercise: «In hot weather children can become dehydrated quickly, with headache, tiredness and dizziness as the first signs.» You feel dizzy on a hot day. What should you do? | Run faster to cool down | *Stop, sit in the shade, drink water and tell an adult | Lie in the sun to get a tan | Keep playing and ignore it
exercise: Which of these can cause dizziness? | *Spinning round and round for a long time | Reading a book quietly in a chair | Drinking a glass of water after playing | Smiling at a friend
test: «Headache, dizziness, double vision or feeling odd after a knock can be concussion.» After a knock on the head, you feel dizziness. What should you do? | Have a drink of cola and carry on | Spin round to check your balance | Keep going and see if it goes away | *Tell an adult straight away
test: Which phrase uses dizziness correctly? | more dizzy than a dizziness | *a spell of dizziness | a dizzinesses of the room | dizzinesses and headaches
exam: In science, what does the inner ear help with, and what can spinning do to it? | Hearing only; spinning makes it louder | Seeing colours; spinning makes them brighter | Digestion; spinning speeds it up | *Balance; spinning confuses it and can cause dizziness
